  "fact_notes": [
    "オリジナル教材。人物や出来事は架空の例であり、実在の事業・調査・実証結果ではない。制作台帳は来歴確認用。"
  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Two students named Ali and Hana are working together on a school poster.",
          "ja": "アリとハナという二人の生徒が学校のポスターを共同制作している。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Hana sends Ali a photograph of a possible design and asks for his opinion.",
          "ja": "ハナはデザイン候補の写真を送りアリの意見を尋ねる。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Ali replies with a short message saying that it is fine.",
          "ja": "アリは問題ないという短いメッセージを返す。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Hana worries that her partner is disappointed because his answer contains no further comments.",
          "ja": "ハナは返答に追加の意見がないため相手が失望しているのではと心配する。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "At their next meeting, Hana asks whether Ali would prefer her to prepare a completely different design.",
          "ja": "次の会合でハナは全く違うデザインを準備した方がよいか尋ねる。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Ali is surprised because he thought his reply had clearly expressed approval.",
          "ja": "アリは返答が承認を明確に表したと思っていたので驚く。"
        },
        {
          "en": "He explains that he was traveling home when the message arrived and had little time to write a detailed response.",
          "ja": "メッセージが届いた時は帰宅途中で詳細な返答を書く時間がほとんどなかったと説明する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The students discover that the same brief reply can be interpreted in different ways.",
          "ja": "同じ短い返答も異なる方法で解釈され得ると二人は発見する。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "They discuss what information is available during a face-to-face conversation but may be absent from a written message.",
          "ja": "対面会話では利用できるが書面メッセージでは欠ける情報について議論する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A speaker's expression and tone of voice can sometimes help a listener understand the intention behind particular words.",
          "ja": "話し手の表情や声の調子は特定の語の背後の意図を聞き手が理解する助けになる場合がある。"
        },
        {
          "en": "However, these signals can also be misunderstood during direct conversations.",
          "ja": "しかしこうした合図も直接会話で誤解され得る。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Neither method of communication guarantees that the participants will understand each other perfectly.",
          "ja": "どちらの意思疎通方法も参加者が互いを完全に理解することを保証しない。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Ali and Hana agree to use more specific comments when discussing important design choices.",
          "ja": "重要なデザイン選択を議論する際はより具体的なコメントを使うことに同意する。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They also decide to ask for clarification when a reply seems unexpected rather than immediately assuming a negative intention.",
          "ja": "返答が予想外に思える場合はすぐ否定的意図を想定せず説明を求めることも決める。"
        },
        {
          "en": "This arrangement does not require them to write a long explanation every time they exchange a message.",
          "ja": "この仕組みはメッセージ交換のたびに長い説明を書くことを求めない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "It simply gives them a way to address uncertainty before it influences their shared work.",
          "ja": "不確実性が共同作業に影響する前に対処する方法を提供するだけだ。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Communication involves both expressing an idea and interpreting the information that another person provides.",
          "ja": "意思疎通には考えの表現と他者が提供する情報の解釈が伴う。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A misunderstanding need not indicate that either person intended to cause a problem.",
          "ja": "誤解はどちらかが問題を引き起こす意図を持ったことを示す必要はない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Asking a thoughtful question can reveal information that was previously missing.",
          "ja": "思慮深い質問は以前欠けていた情報を明らかにし得る。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The message becomes clearer when both students are willing to examine their assumptions.",
          "ja": "双方が前提を調べる意欲を持つとメッセージはより明確になる。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
